WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.228
Host: Explain how a meal containing fat and
acid can recruit different pancreatic
responses.

2
00:00:06.228 --> 00:00:11.582
Guide: Duodenal acid stimulates secretin and
bicarbonate-rich ductal secretion.

3
00:00:11.582 --> 00:00:20.655
Guide: Fat and protein products stimulate
cholecystokinin and enzyme-rich secretion,
with neural signals coordinating the response.

4
00:00:20.655 --> 00:00:25.464
Guide: The pathways interact rather than
operating as isolated switches.

5
00:00:25.464 --> 00:00:31.642
Host: Fat enters the duodenum. Which
coordinated response fits its digestion?

6
00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:36.631
Guide: CCK supporting enzyme secretion and
gallbladder contraction.

7
00:00:36.631 --> 00:00:42.224
Guide: CCK helps match enzyme and bile
delivery to the incoming nutrient load.
